Renewing a Cameroonian passport is a straightforward process that begins with an online registration and ends with the collection of the new document. The passport remains valid for five years and can be renewed even before it expires [Article 5] [Article 6].

You start by **creating a pre‑enrollment file on the PassCam portal (passcam.cm)**, paying the issuance fee of 110 000 FCFA electronically (MoMo, Orange Money, or credit card) and scheduling an appointment for the biometric enrolment [Étape 1]. 

On the day of the appointment you attend the enrolment centre, where you will present the following documents: 

- receipt of the fee payment; 
- a certified true copy of your birth certificate; 
- a certified true copy of your national identity card; 
- a proof of profession, if applicable; 
- for applicants residing abroad, a certified true copy of a residence permit or equivalent; 
- for married women, a certified true copy of the marriage certificate; 
- a certified true copy of the naturalisation or reintegration decree, if applicable; 
- the loss certificate of the previous passport, if applicable. 

These pieces are required by law [Article 12, alinéa 3].

After the biometric capture, the authorities produce the new passport. You will be **notified by SMS and email when it is ready**, and you may collect it yourself or authorize a third party with a duly legalized power of attorney [Étape 4].

Remember that you remain fully responsible for the accuracy and completeness of the information and documents you submit. If any of the required pieces are missing, the request cannot be processed.
